7. The nurse conducting a sleep workshop in the community would identify which patients to be at 
risk for obstructive sleep apnea (OSA)? (Select all that apply.) 
a. Deviated septum 
b. Recessed chin 
c. Alcohol use 
d. Large neck 
e. Recent tonsillectomy 
ANS: A, B, C, D 
Risk factors for OSA include obesity, large neck circumference, smoking, alcohol use, and a family 
history of OSA. Structural abnormalities such as a recessed chin, abnormal 
upper-airway structures, deviated septum, nasal polyps, or enlarged tonsils can predispose a 
person to OSA. 
 
